risk_desc:
This product poses a risk of injury because:

- there is no second breaking system;

- there is no safety guard set on the chain;

- contrary to requirements, space between stabilizer and rear wheel is less then 175mm;

- metal elements all over the frame have sharp and abrasive edges;

- contrary to requirements, protrusion of the screws fastening the mudguard on the front wheel and the ends of the break holders is more then 8cm long;

- fastening screws are not rounded at the ends.
In addition, concentration of the lead and chromium in the orange paint is higher then limits laid down in European Standard EN 71-3 and the product thereby poses a chemical risk.

This product poses a serious risk of release of metals for the following reasons:


- migration of lead from the red label between one and three times the maximum limit authorised;


- migration of lead from the red and green paint of the sleigh over three times the maximum limit authorised;


- migration of chromium from the green paint of the sleigh over three times the maximum limit authorised.


This toy does not comply with the Toys Directive and the relevant European standard EN 71.

The product poses a serious risk of:


- burns because the average rate of spread of flame of the cap of the costume is 17.5 mm/s, while the maximum rate permitted is 10 mm/s;


- choking because the foam in the cap is accessible from the inside of the same and pieces easily become detached, producing small parts which fits into the small parts cylinder. Pieces of the imitation leather belt, the red feather in the cap broke and the rivets on the front of the shirt also become detached easily, producing small parts which fit into the small parts cylinder;


- suffocation because the thickness of the bag, which has an opening perimeter greater than 380 mm, is 0.035+/-0.005 mm.


The toy does not comply with the Toys Directive and the European standard EN 71-1.

This product poses:



- a risk of choking because small parts come off during the tension test. All parts fit wholly within the small parts cylinder. Children may put small elements into mouth and choke;



- a risk of suffocation, because it contains a cord which thickness is smaller than 1,5 mm;



- a chemical risk because red paint contains 630 mg/kg of lead (Pb) and 130 mg/kg of chromium (Cr). 



The product does not comply with Toys Directive and the relevant European standards EN 71-1 and EN 71-3.

